- `i=2`: `data[2]=1 != max_val=2`, `current_count=2 > max_count=1` → `max_count=2`, `max_val=data[1]=2`, `current_count=1`
- `i=3`: `data[3]=1 != max_val=2`, `current_count=1 > max_count=2`? No → `current_count=1`
- `i=4`: `data[4]=1 != max_val=2`, `current_count=1 > max_count=2`? No → `current_count=1`
- End: returns `(2, 2)` — wrong. The final run of three `1`s was never evaluated.

The fix: after the loop, compare the final `current_count` against `max_count` and update if needed.

<solution language="rust" verdict="fix">
fn longest_streak(data: &Vec<i32>) -> (i32, usize) {
    let mut max_val = data[0];
    let mut max_count: usize = 1;
    let mut current_count: usize = 1;

    for i in 1..data.len() {
        if data[i] == max_val {
            current_count += 1;
        } else if current_count > max_count {
            max_count = current_count;
            max_val = data[i - 1];
            current_count = 1;
        } else {
            current_count = 1;
        }
    }
    if current_count > max_count {
        max_count = current_count;
        max_val = data[data.len() - 1];
    }
    (max_val, max_count)
}
